A||||10||Dan86gt3.8||Has anyone ever ben busted for street racing?||||5||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||02-24-2000||05:10 PM||||Hey I was at my home town (waco) this past weekend, and we went out to a little two lane highway and were doing some racing.  Well about 10 races went buy and a car rolled up, turned out it was a sheriff.  Well he asked everyone if they had beer and checked the people that were drivings lisences (actually just looked at them, and then let us go with a "better not catch yall out here no mo"  this was a redneck sheriff that was operating off the good old boy system so I gues we lucked out.  Has anyone not ben as lucky as me?||||reg||5
Z||000001||wkayl||02-24-2000||06:26 PM||||Back in ought six (actually it was 1975) I had a 71 Challenger RT with the best options you could have (2 young ladies).  After a Mustang nailed it from 3 stoplights and me just driving away like a gentleman, one of the young ladies said "Your not going to let a mustang do that to you, are you?"  Well, my manhood was being questioned so at the next light he found out what all 383 cubic inches and 4 speed would do.  Half a block into it I saw the familiar flashing (lights that is) in my mirror.  To make this already too long of a story shorter, my yes Sirs and no Sirs must have worked. I got a 10 mph over the limit ticket. I asked why he stoped me and not the Mustang?  He said "He was loosing, maybe he won't do it again and I got you so I know you WON"T do it again, will you?"   HEHEHE ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||02-24-2000||11:08 PM||||This isn't exactly about street racing, but close enough... When I was in high school, we used to have burnout contests in the parking lot. I had been sitting in the same spot for about 10 seconds, with smoke boiling out from under the right wheelwell, (holding the brake, gas floorboarded, "open" rear end), when I looked in my mirror and saw the rotating blue lights shining through the smoke. Not only did I get a ticket, but I broke one of my spider gears (among other things) into four pieces. My dad was *most unhappy*. I was driving a 68 Ford Fairlane with a stock (except for the glasspacks) 302. Sorry about the use of the "F" word.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||02-25-2000||12:19 AM||||hey, im thinkin about buying a 1976 Ford Mustang with a 302 V-8 to do some burnouts!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIEROCIOUS||02-25-2000||06:54 AM||||I raced for three years in my 73 Nova!<P>52 tickets.....<P>2 stuck........<P>5 mph over.....<P>and lack of mudflaps.....120.00<P>I pleaded guilty on....<P>2 of my tickets.......<P>guess wich ones.......<P>LOL......<P>If you ever get a ticket fight it you'll win!<BR>If you want I can tell you stories all day and night! Those were the days....sigh!||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||02-25-2000||09:25 AM||||I was watching some dork who borrowed his moms Chevy Caprice do some donuts in the high school parking lot one afternoon, until he hit a light pole. That was hilarious.<P>I also watched some guy do a neutral drop in his little dodge pickup.  The transmission ended up in pieces. That one was pretty cool.<P>One of my friends felt the need to pass a car in a no passing zone one day, and he just loved to rev the engine in his V6 camaro.  The spot he picked to pass was in front of a police officers house, who just happened to be outside playing ball with his kid.  The officer heard the engine revving and saw the car go by, next thing you know my friend had a ticket for "Willfull Wanton Reckless Driving" and Racing. That was a very expensive mistake, but he got what he deserved.  <P>I got a hand slap from a game warden for taking my 1978 Olds Delta 88 out to a management area and doing a bit o mudding.  Had I not ended up with the car in the ditch, he would have never known the difference.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||02-25-2000||11:38 AM||||Fierocious... Only two out of 52 stuck?!? That's some serious harassment. Sounds like they *really didn't like* you. <BR>As for neutral drops.. Knew a guy with a 73 340 Duster. Usta do neutral drops all the time. Till he left his transmission in a smoking pile of parts in the middle of the street. (Something about Mopar trannies?) The guy was a complete fool, though. Drove the $#!+ out of that car. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spyder||02-25-2000||12:11 PM||||In 1987 had a 87 V8 firebird and I was 17 years dumb, I mean old.  I did a 75 foot burnout in front of 200+ people that were in a parking lot.  It was beautiful. Then I said “showed my arse, time to go home”. I made it a block and noticed a small, small blue light behind me.  It was a motorcycle cop. (at least it wasn’t a cushman) I luckily got out of it.<P>Another time same car, raced a 300ZX, I spun wheels and got him off the line, then I noticed Mr. Officer, pull in behind from a side street, I hoped he didn’t see what happened. I turned off, and he followed me, so then he pulled me over.  Got away with a warning.<P>I have been good lately, not really, just smarter.<BR>Choose your races.<BR>Don’t spin wheels.<BR>Don’t do it around lots of people.<BR>I’ll probably get a ticket now, since I voiced my opinion.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||02-26-2000||02:16 AM||||Oh baby! STREET RACING stories.  I actually only race when there is almost NO cars in sight(not very often.)  The only ticket I ever got was for street racing.  About 2 years ago, I just got my '84 Z28 H.O. camaro. My first night cruizin, I run into this prick in a white 98 Mustang GT.  We play around a little trying to out-accelerate each other, and I swear my H.O. could pull harder.  GM rated that 305 H.O. at 190 HP, but various sources have said that THAT engine(L69) was highly under-rated. Apart from that, I was running advanced timing and a tweaked Edelbrock 600 with 3.73 gears in the rear. So.... We come to the light and there doesn't seem too be any cars in sight except for a blue 4-door behind me.  I glanced back to check for a light-bar, and I didnt' see one.  So it turn green, and I start the biggest smoke show I'd ever accomplished!  The mustang got almost 0 wheelspin and took off without me.  An instant later, there's blue lights in the rear-view mirror. DAMN!  It was an unmarked cop car.  I got a 70 dollar ticket for exhibition driving, and the Rustang never got pulled over. oh well....<P>later all,<BR>Da Bastard ||||reg||14
Z||000009||batboy||02-26-2000||08:42 AM||||I came as close to getting busted as I ever want way back in Des Moines, Iowa on "the loop" in 1982. It was because I was showing off in front of people. I violated one of Spyder's rules (which are good common sense). I only got off by "yes, sir this, yes sir that" and by pointing out that when I reached the speed limit I quit racing and the other guy (who got away) kept on driving like a bat out of hell. I beat the dude out of the hole and then immediately shut down. Those Chevy big blocks do make a lot of noise and the N-50 Mickey Thompson rear tires probably did squeal a bit (ok a lot). I never saw the cop until the cherries popped on. I learned a lot that night. No racing on city streets! After that, I went back to racing only on lonely two lane blacktop roads when I had the need for speed. With more traffic nowadays, it better and safer just to go to the dragstrip and make several passes in one evening for about $10 or less.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||02-26-2000||09:16 PM||||Hey batboy we were all out on a "lolely" 2 lane blacktop it hooks great (all though I never have "traction problems").  The cop was asking what we wered doing out there in b.f.e, like he couldn't figure out what about 15 mustangs and 10 fbody's, a gsx eclipse, older 300 zx and a old chevelle that has a big block/rollcage/ and huge slicks out back, were doing on the side of his blacktop 2 laner in the middle of nowhere with about 30 random burnout marks right by where we were parked hmmm.... I wonder what was going on????? like he had to ask.||||reg||12
